--[[
Preview: pictures, PDF documents and Markdown files, looked at and not
changed, as a Mac's Preview shows them.

  saule run .              nothing open: asks what to open
  saule run . FILE         that file

    model   the document (Document), a picture in memory (Picture), a
            Markdown file as blocks of text (Markdown), a PDF's pages
            (Pages), and how what is shown is zoomed and moved (Viewing)
    views   the window: a bar, and under it the picture, the page or the
            formatted text

A PDF's pages are drawn by `saule-pdf` (saule-linux's `pdf/`), a page at a
time as it is turned to. Where that program is missing, on another system,
a PDF cannot be shown and the window says so.
]]

from PreviewApp import PreviewApp

class Main
  static fn main()
    PreviewApp().run()
  end
end
